==Finnish==
{{wikipedia|lang=fi}}
{{Finnish index|k|i}}

===Etymology===
From the same {{proto|Finno-Ugric|kiwe|lang=fi}} as Hungarian {{term|kő}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|lang=fi|[ˈkiʋi]}}
* {{rhymes|iʋi|lang=fi}}
* {{hyphenation|ki|vi}}

===Noun===
{{infl|fi|noun}}

# A [[stone]].
# Any piece of [[stone]] which is larger than a grain of sand.
# A [[rock]] as a relatively small mass of stone projecting out of ground.
# A [[boulder]].
# A general term for solid, mineral-based construction materials, such as [[brick]], [[concrete]] or natural stone.
# {{nautical|informal|lang=fi}} An underwater [[rock]] which bay be dangerous for seafarers.
# A short form of {{term|jalokivi}}; a [[rock]], [[jewel]].
#: ''Tässä kellossa on 17 '''kiveä'''''.
#:: This clockwork is made with 17 '''jewels'''.
#: ''Katso tuota '''kiveä''' hänen sormessaan!'' 
#:: Look at that '''rock''' in her finger!

