====Usage notes====
A large mass of stone projecting out of ground is called {{term|kallio}}. Also, if the stone mass is known or assumed to be part of [[bedrock]], it's called {{term|kallio}}, even if the visible part is small. Similarly, if a large stone mass is known not to be part of bedrock, it may be called {{term|kivi|lang=fi}} or {{term|lohkare}}.

